@startuml
title GeoVisLM Deployment Components

skinparam componentStyle rectangle
skinparam shadowing false

package "Ingress" {
  actor "Browser User" as User
  component "Cloudflare" as Cloudflare
  component "Cloudflare Access\noptional perimeter" as Access
  component "Caddy\nReverse Proxy" as Caddy
}

package "Docker Compose Stack" {
  component "Dashboard API + HTML UI\nFastAPI" as Dashboard
  component "First-Party Auth\nlogin / signup / session cookie" as Auth
  component "Projects + Memberships\ncomments + audit events" as Collaboration
  component "Worker Service\npolls queued jobs" as Worker
  database "PostGIS\nmetadata, runs, files, outputs" as Database
  folder "Shared Output Storage\nprojects / runs / jobs / artifacts" as Storage
  queue "File-Backed Job Queue\noutputs/jobs/*/job.json" as Jobs
}

User --> Cloudflare
Cloudflare --> Access
Access --> Caddy
Caddy --> Dashboard

Dashboard --> Auth
Dashboard --> Collaboration
Dashboard --> Database : optional structured metadata
Dashboard --> Storage : persisted uploads, runs, reports
Dashboard --> Jobs : create queued job record

Worker --> Jobs : claim next queued job
Worker --> Storage : read inputs / write artifacts
Worker --> Database : optional status metadata

Collaboration --> Storage : member, comment, audit JSON
Collaboration --> Database : optional project metadata

note right of Jobs
The dashboard does not call the worker directly.
The durable boundary is the persisted job record
and shared storage.
end note

@enduml
